,192,215,245,275,321,357],{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":27,"primary":29,"id":50,"slice_type":51,"slice_label":30},"pageHeaderNoCta","sktwi1xtmkfgx8626",[28],{},{"theme":30,"PageHeaderTitle":31,"PageHeaderText":32,"PageHeaderImage":37,"heroImage":48,"videoContent":49,"showPremiumLogo":30},null,"How to package clothes for shipping",[33],{"type":34,"text":35,"spans":36},"paragraph","",[],{"dimensions":38,"alt":41,"copyright":30,"url":42,"id":43,"edit":44},{"width":39,"height":40},300,65,"Wrap","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002Fa76e9a48-a69a-4059-8184-2c60875ba1a4_wrap.svg","YhYpMRIAACkA0QCA",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":47},0,1,"#fff",{},{"link_type":19},"page_header$685be352-9a1d-4aca-9374-66032117e119","page_header",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":54,"primary":56,"id":85,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},"default-slice",[55],{},{"CardImage":57,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":67,"CardText":68,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":83,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":58,"alt":61,"copyright":30,"url":62,"id":63,"edit":64},{"width":59,"height":60},1000,667,"A customer is crouched on the floor of their apartment, holding items in one hand and is about to place them in the box in front of them.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6XrypbqstJ9-WeK_EVRI_LOCATION_04_5211.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6XrypbqstJ9-WeK",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"transparent","none","Packaging clothes",[69],{"type":34,"text":70,"spans":71,"direction":82},"Whether you're selling your clothes online or sending an outfit to a loved one, when packaging clothes for shipping, the contents need to be as protected as possible. Here are our best tips for folding, wrapping and padding clothes correctly.",[72,80],{"start":73,"end":74,"type":75,"data":76},15,42,"hyperlink",{"link_type":77,"url":78,"target":79},"Web","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-sell-clothes-online","_self",{"start":73,"end":74,"type":81},"strong","ltr",{"link_type":84},"Any","card$029aa8ea-3ecc-478a-85af-6309a7c0a4aa","card",{"variation":88,"version":26,"items":89,"primary":115,"id":118,"slice_type":119,"slice_label":30},"listComponent",[90,103],{"title":91,"content":92,"icon":96},"Don’t roll clothes",[93],{"type":34,"text":94,"spans":95},"Always fold them to save space",[],{"dimensions":97,"alt":99,"copyright":30,"url":100,"id":101,"edit":102},{"width":98,"height":98},40,"Clothes in a box icon","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002F310e5f30-345e-45c1-a5cb-91a5eceee8ae_What%27s+in+the+box.svg","Yh96FxIAACoA-ZsT",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":47},{"title":104,"content":105,"icon":109},"Always fold clothes carefully",[106],{"type":34,"text":107,"spans":108},"To avoid creases, which is especially important for a business sending clothing",[],{"dimensions":110,"alt":111,"copyright":30,"url":112,"id":113,"edit":114},{"width":98,"height":98},"Icon of a parcel","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002F8321288c-05db-46b8-9767-db5da18fbfae_parcel1.svg","Yh96FhIAAC4A-Zr2",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":47},{"theme":30,"title":116,"description":117},"Posting clothes with Evri","To ship clothing, your items need to fit in the packaging you’re sending them in, so they arrive safely at their destination.\n\nOur two top tips are:","list_block$731388bf-2f56-43ed-800c-5e6504ce8d40","list_block",{"variation":121,"version":26,"items":122,"primary":124,"id":136,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},"cardWithImageNoCta",[123],{},{"CardImage":125,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":131,"CardText":132,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":126,"alt":127,"copyright":30,"url":128,"id":129,"edit":130},{"width":59,"height":60},"A mother is placing a pair of jeans into a parcel box with the shipping label sat beside ready to attach. Her to children are reading a book on the sofa behind her.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6zc6JbqstJ9-inN_EVRI_LOCATION_05_7582.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6zc6JbqstJ9-inN",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"Use sturdy packaging",[133],{"type":34,"text":134,"spans":135},"These are some of the best types of packaging to use when sending clothes through our system.",[],"card$35af011d-c3b9-4915-8eb5-2e4ae421c00c",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":138,"primary":140,"id":156,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},[139],{},{"CardImage":141,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":147,"CardText":148,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":155,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":142,"alt":143,"copyright":30,"url":144,"id":145,"edit":146},{"width":59,"height":60},"An older woman is wrapping a parcel. She is pressing down on the label to keep it flat.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6owgJbqstJ9-cUr_EVRI_LOCATION_06_10345.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6owgJbqstJ9-cUr",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"1. Padded envelopes",[149,152],{"type":34,"text":150,"spans":151},"For a single item of clothing, buy a padded envelope and pop the item in the sleeve. This is a cost-effective way of sending smaller items, as it’s a lightweight choice. ",[],{"type":34,"text":153,"spans":154},"Then, seal it with the adhesive tape attached, and stick the shipping label to the parcel.",[],{"link_type":84},"card$7c384756-b7b8-434b-8646-d1a462d83cd4",{"variation":158,"version":26,"items":159,"primary":172,"id":174,"slice_type":119,"slice_label":30},"listNoIcon",[160,164,169],{"title":161,"content":162,"isNumbered":163},"Inside padding in padded envelopes helps secure clothing",[],true,{"title":165,"content":166,"isNumbered":163},"Choose from different-sized padded envelopes",[167],{"type":34,"text":35,"spans":168},[],{"title":170,"content":171,"isNumbered":163},"They're great for sending smaller items.",[],{"theme":30,"title":173,"description":30,"showPaddingTop":21},"Advantages of padded envelopes for clothing","list_block$e3664b9a-7fb3-491c-9068-07af01e279f6",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":176,"primary":178,"id":191,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},[177],{},{"CardImage":179,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":185,"CardText":186,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":190,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":180,"alt":181,"copyright":30,"url":182,"id":183,"edit":184},{"width":59,"height":60},"A mother is placing a pair of jeans into a parcel bag with the shipping label sat beside ready to attach. Her to children are watching a tablet on the sofa behind her.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6zc85bqstJ9-inT_EVRI_LOCATION_05_7633.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=1%2C0%2C7498%2C5001&w=1000&h=667","Z6zc85bqstJ9-inT",{"x":46,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"2. Plastic delivery bags",[187],{"type":34,"text":188,"spans":189},"When you’re packaging clothes for shipping, plastic mailing bags are a convenient choice - so long as you’re not including more “fragile” clothing.",[],{"link_type":84},"card$f0b90d0a-0f91-47f4-ab82-d50e5c01340a",{"variation":158,"version":26,"items":193,"primary":212,"id":214,"slice_type":119,"slice_label":30},[194,200,206],{"title":195,"content":196,"isNumbered":163},"Really affordable to buy",[197],{"type":34,"text":198,"spans":199},"Saving on overall shipping costs.",[],{"title":201,"content":202,"isNumbered":163},"Less protective",[203],{"type":34,"text":204,"spans":205},"So, avoid using this packaging for more delicate items.",[],{"title":207,"content":208,"isNumbered":163},"Great for light clothing",[209],{"type":34,"text":210,"spans":211},"Such as t-shirts, socks, lingerie, light shirts and dresses.",[],{"theme":30,"title":213,"description":30,"showPaddingTop":21},"Plastic delivery bags are:","list_block$5e196df2-f71d-48c6-8f30-08d46170b1a2",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":216,"primary":218,"id":244,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},[217],{},{"CardImage":219,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":225,"CardText":226,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":243,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":220,"alt":221,"copyright":30,"url":222,"id":223,"edit":224},{"width":59,"height":60},"A mother is placing the lid on a parcel box with the shipping label attached so it is ready to send. Her two children are sat on the sofa behind her reading a book.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6zc65bqstJ9-inP_EVRI_LOCATION_05_7587.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6zc65bqstJ9-inP",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"3. Cardboard boxes",[227,237,240],{"type":34,"text":228,"spans":229,"direction":82},"For packaging larger clothes, or bulk sending clothes, cardboard boxes are a really great choice. ",[230,236],{"start":231,"end":232,"type":75,"data":233},33,45,{"link_type":77,"url":234,"target":235},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Four-services\u002Fbulk-send","_blank",{"start":231,"end":232,"type":81},{"type":34,"text":238,"spans":239,"direction":82},"Just choose a box that’s slightly bigger than the clothes you’re sending! This makes room for extra packaging materials, like bubble wrap or scrunched-up newspaper, to stop things moving around.",[],{"type":34,"text":241,"spans":242,"direction":82}," ",[],{"link_type":84},"card$7cb6b0a4-1b80-4c48-b84f-0e1e1d385e4c",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":246,"primary":248,"id":274,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},[247],{},{"CardImage":249,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":255,"CardText":256,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":273,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":250,"alt":251,"copyright":30,"url":252,"id":253,"edit":254},{"width":59,"height":60},"A close-up of a customer's hands as they are crouched on the floor of their apartment, holding items the lid of a box, ready to seal their parcel in front of them.","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6Xr85bqstJ9-WeM_EVRI_LOCATION_04_5235.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6Xr85bqstJ9-WeM",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"Cardboard boxes for shipping clothing are",[257,261,264],{"type":258,"text":259,"spans":260,"direction":82},"list-item","Great for sending a larger amount of clothes.",[],{"type":258,"text":262,"spans":263,"direction":82},"Protective, sturdy and durable.",[],{"type":258,"text":265,"spans":266,"direction":82},"Recyclable - a great eco-friendly packaging option, with the person receiving the item able to reuse it. ",[267,272],{"start":268,"end":269,"type":75,"data":270},21,43,{"link_type":77,"url":271,"target":79},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Feverything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging",{"start":268,"end":269,"type":81},{"link_type":84},"card$5966f1ab-f7c5-428b-a914-6490df732449",{"variation":158,"version":26,"items":276,"primary":318,"id":320,"slice_type":119,"slice_label":30},[277,280,286,289,295,298,304],{"title":278,"content":279,"isNumbered":163},"Fold the items neatly",[],{"title":281,"content":282,"isNumbered":163},"Wrap tissue paper around the clothing",[283],{"type":34,"text":284,"spans":285},"This gives added protection.",[],{"title":287,"content":288,"isNumbered":163},"Seal the tissue paper with a sticker\u002Ftape",[],{"title":290,"content":291,"isNumbered":163},"Insert extra padding, like bubble wrap",[292],{"type":34,"text":293,"spans":294},"This helps cushion the items.",[],{"title":296,"content":297,"isNumbered":163},"Place the protected clothes inside the box",[],{"title":299,"content":300,"isNumbered":163},"Use parcel tape to seal the box",[301],{"type":34,"text":302,"spans":303},"Make sure you tape every corner to keep clothes nice and secure.",[],{"title":305,"content":306,"isNumbered":163},"Add the shipping label to the box",[307],{"type":34,"text":308,"spans":309},"This can be either printed for a Courier collection or at an Evri ParcelShop\u002FLocker. Just use our ParcelShop finder to find locations offering this service. ",[310,313],{"start":311,"end":312,"type":81},97,116,{"start":314,"end":315,"type":75,"data":316},98,115,{"link_type":77,"url":317},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Ffind-a-parcelshop?printInStore=true#\u002F",{"theme":30,"title":319,"description":30,"showPaddingTop":21},"Once you’ve found the best sized cardboard box for your clothes, simply:","list_block$86de776e-7f3c-4fbc-9689-0afd4d496bf5",{"variation":322,"version":26,"items":323,"primary":325,"id":356,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},"cardNoImageWithCta",[324],{},{"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":326,"CardText":327,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":355,"IsEco":21},"Consider extra packaging for delicate clothes",[328,346,349,352],{"type":34,"text":329,"spans":330},"Most clothes aren’t fragile, but some pieces might require more care than others. This includes items like beaded jumpers or a silk designer suit, for example. Some clothing falls under our prohibited items, too. For instance, you can’t send real fur through our network.",[331,334],{"start":332,"end":333,"type":81},189,206,{"start":335,"end":333,"type":75,"data":336},190,{"id":337,"type":338,"tags":339,"lang":16,"slug":341,"first_publication_date":342,"last_publication_date":343,"uid":344,"url":345,"link_type":19,"isBroken":21},"YhZhMBIAACgA0bfU","content-page",[340],"Send a Parcel","uk-destinations","2022-02-23T16:30:45+0000","2025-10-14T10:34:12+0000","what-i-can-and-cannot-send","\u002Fsend\u002Fwhat-i-can-and-cannot-send",{"type":34,"text":347,"spans":348},"Packaging fragile items requires extra packaging, so:",[],{"type":258,"text":350,"spans":351},"Add filled packaging, like bubble wrap and newspaper.",[],{"type":258,"text":353,"spans":354},"Wrap bubble wrap around zips, beads, or more delicate embellishments.",[],{"link_type":84},"card$04efa7d3-c483-4164-bb9e-1c1a4e6d209a",{"variation":121,"version":26,"items":358,"primary":360,"id":404,"slice_type":86,"slice_label":30},[359],{},{"CardImage":361,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":367,"CardText":368,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":362,"alt":363,"copyright":30,"url":364,"id":365,"edit":366},{"width":59,"height":60},"Customer carrying multiple parcels inside a ParcelShop store, ready to drop off for delivery","how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R1D5bqstJ9-SOx_EVRI_LOCATION_03_2468.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6R1D5bqstJ9-SOx",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"Send your parcel",[369,389],{"type":34,"text":370,"spans":371},"Now you know how to package clothes for shipping, you’ll feel confident doing this in future! All that’s left to do is send your parcel. Simply find a ParcelShop that’s convenient for you, book a Courier collection, or choose a Locker to take your clothes package to. ",[372,375,378,380,383,386],{"start":373,"end":374,"type":81},144,161,{"start":373,"end":374,"type":75,"data":376},{"link_type":77,"url":377},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Ffind-a-parcelshop?parcelShops=true#\u002F",{"start":332,"end":379,"type":81},214,{"start":332,"end":379,"type":75,"data":381},{"link_type":77,"url":382},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Four-services\u002Fcourier-service",{"start":384,"end":385,"type":81},228,234,{"start":384,"end":385,"type":75,"data":387},{"link_type":77,"url":388},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fparcelshops\u002Flockers",{"type":34,"text":390,"spans":391},"For further advice on sending parcels, read through our guides section, where you can discover helpful tips on how to package books and more. ",[392,395,398,401],{"start":393,"end":394,"type":81},52,62,{"start":393,"end":394,"type":75,"data":396},{"link_type":77,"url":397},"how-to-package-clothes-for-shipping.html\u002F\